<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Turkish War (1768–1774)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1768">1768</a>–<a href="/years/1774">1774</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as First Russo-Turkish War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Turkish War of 1768–1774 was a conflict between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Russian forces won major victories on land and at sea, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kucuk-kaynarca">Treaty of Küçük Kaynarca</a> ended the war by granting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> access to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and making the Crimean Khanate independent of Ottoman control. Accounts of the Russian Empire treat it as a key stage in Russia's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nam-tien">southward expansion</a>.</p></div>
